                    <note type="editorial"/>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>This is probably John Cozens, Norwich grocer and radical. There are 
several references to him in Jewson's <title>Jacobin City</title> - including that he succeeded <persName key="TAY03">William Taylor</persName> as Secretary 
to the Norwich Revolution Society and that <persName key="THE01">Thelwall</persName> lectured from the windows above his shop.
As this meeting takes place during Godwin's visit to Norwich in 1796, this seems a likely identification.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"> C.B. Jewson, <title>The Jacobin City: A Portrait of Norwich in its Reaction to the French Revolution 1788-1802</title> (Glasgow: Blackie, 1975)</bibl>
